00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.200
Acme insurance incorporated offers affordable health insurance to thousands

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.600
of customers all over the United States.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:34.200
And as the lead data scientist at Acme, you are tasked with creating an automated

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:40.600
system to estimate the annual medical expenditure for new customers using

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:46.100
information such as their age, sex, BMI, children, smoking habits,

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.900
region of residents, et cetera.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.600
Why are you asked to do that?

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.400
Because estimates from your system will be used to determine the annual

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.400
insurance premium, which is the amount paid every month or every year.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.000
That is offered to the customer.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.200
So your job is to figure out when a new customer applies for medical

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:13.000
insurance based on information like their age, sex, BMI, et cetera, how much

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.600
they might incur in medical bills in an average year.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.900
If you can find that information along with some other information can

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:28.000
be used to determine what you should charge the customer for insurance.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.300
And this is a typical problem that you will face and it's a typical example

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.800
of a machine learning problem where you want to replace some manual decision

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:42.600
making or one, one piece of a manual decision making process with some automation.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.400
So in this case, for example, you may need an expert who has seen customers

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.900
for several decades to figure out based on this information, what their medical

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.900
