00:45:41.400 --> 00:45:45.400
And one last thing I want to mention is the correlation versus causation policy.

00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:51.400
Note that a high correlation cannot be used to interpret a cause effect relationship between features.

00:45:51.400 --> 00:45:58.400
Two features X and Y can be correlated if X causes Y or if Y causes X.

00:45:58.400 --> 00:46:00.400
You can see that in the formula.

00:46:00.400 --> 00:46:03.400
If you replace X with Y and Y with X, nothing changes.

00:46:03.400 --> 00:46:04.400
It's the same formula.

00:46:04.400 --> 00:46:09.400
If you flip the axis here, nothing changes the relationship remains the same.

00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:13.400
So it does not give you a direction to interpret causation in.

00:46:13.400 --> 00:46:14.400
Okay.

00:46:14.400 --> 00:46:15.400
That's very important.

00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:22.400
X could cause Y or Y could cause X or it's possible that both are caused independently by some other factor Z.

00:46:22.400 --> 00:46:24.400
And the correlation will no longer hold true.

00:46:24.400 --> 00:46:29.400
If one of those cause effect relationships is broken, like if Z causes X and Z causes Y.

00:46:29.400 --> 00:46:36.400
But if you fix or change whatever effect Z has on Y, then X and Y will no longer be correlated.

00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:40.400
So that's why I do not interpret cause effect relationships from correlations.

00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:46.400
It's easy and a lot of people do it, even though it seems obvious, a lot of people do it, but it's wrong.

00:46:46.400 --> 00:46:55.400
Just to give you an example, for example, if you let's say created a scatter plot between race and income,

00:46:55.400 --> 00:47:00.400
you would find that maybe a certain race has lower income and a certain race has higher income.

00:47:00.400 --> 00:47:06.400
And if you want to create a cause effect relationship there, you could say that income is a function of race,

00:47:06.400 --> 00:47:08.400
that if you belong to a certain race, you will learn less.

00:47:08.400 --> 00:47:11.400
And then you may read more information into that.

00:47:11.400 --> 00:47:13.400
And that is because of such and such reasons, et cetera.

00:47:13.400 --> 00:47:18.400
But it's possible that this is because of something else entirely.

00:47:18.400 --> 00:47:25.400
For example, racism, systemic racism that may have caused incomes to be lower for a particular race.

00:47:25.400 --> 00:47:31.400
And once you fix that, and maybe if you control for that, if you see people who have not been subjected

00:47:31.400 --> 00:47:37.400
for several generations to racism, you might find that you no longer have the same correlation.

00:47:37.400 --> 00:47:40.400
So try not to read too much into these graphs.

00:47:40.400 --> 00:47:46.400
Always be careful because it's a very natural human tendency to create these interpretations.

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:54.400
And when it becomes even more magnified is when these into these correlations are captured in automated systems.

00:47:54.400 --> 00:47:57.400
Computers cannot differentiate between correlation and causation.

00:47:57.400 --> 00:48:03.400
And decisions based on an automated system can often have major consequences on society.

00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:08.400
So it's important to study why automated systems lead to a given result.

00:48:08.400 --> 00:48:14.400
And again, another example of this, you may have heard about this facial recognition technology developed by Amazon

00:48:14.400 --> 00:48:17.400
is being used in law enforcement.

00:48:17.400 --> 00:48:26.400
And it just so happens that because of the correct, because of the current distribution of people who are incarcerated,

00:48:26.400 --> 00:48:30.400
a certain race has a higher representation in the incarcerated population.

00:48:30.400 --> 00:48:39.400
And so the model is more likely to predict a person with a certain race is a criminal or detect them as a criminal.

00:48:39.400 --> 00:48:42.400
And so more people are likely to be incarcerated from the same race.

00:48:42.400 --> 00:48:47.400
So it can actually aggravate the problems, the problems we have in our human systems.

00:48:47.400 --> 00:48:53.400
And that is why it's very important to be mindful of why we're getting a certain result out of a system that we create

00:48:53.400 --> 00:48:57.400
and realize that determining cause effect relationships requires human insight.

00:48:57.400 --> 00:48:59.400
We shouldn't blindly trust computer systems.

00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:00.400
Okay.

00:49:00.400 --> 00:49:09.400
So that's just my small note about correlation and causation that you should keep in mind.

00:49:09.400 --> 00:49:10.400
