00:51:35.400 --> 00:51:39.400
And a line on the X and Y coordinates has a formula like this.

00:51:39.400 --> 00:51:42.400
A line has a formula Y equals W X plus B.

00:51:42.400 --> 00:51:48.400
So as you make changes to the value of X, the value of Y changes

00:51:48.400 --> 00:51:50.400
and it is determined by two factors.

00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:55.400
So the number W is called the slope and the number B is called the intercept.

00:51:55.400 --> 00:51:56.400
Okay.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:57.400
So what you do is you pick a value for W.

00:51:57.400 --> 00:52:02.200
Let's say you pick that W has the value hundred and you pick a value for B and

00:52:02.200 --> 00:52:05.400
you say B has the value 50.

00:52:05.400 --> 00:52:08.800
And as you change the value of X, the value of Y changes.

00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:13.800
And that is what draws a line on the 2d plane, basic geometry, something you

00:52:13.800 --> 00:52:18.600
would have seen in high school and W is called a slope because it determines how

00:52:18.600 --> 00:52:22.200
much change you will see in Y when you make some change in X.

00:52:22.200 --> 00:52:27.000
So the rate of change of Y with respect to the change in X is W and B is called

00:52:27.000 --> 00:52:31.100
the intercept because B is the value of Y when you set X equals zero.

00:52:31.100 --> 00:52:32.700
So X equals zero means this.

00:52:32.700 --> 00:52:37.700
So that means B is the point at which the line intersects with the Y axis and

00:52:37.700 --> 00:52:39.000
that is called the intercept.

