01:11:35.700 --> 01:11:44.700
And this error is also called a loss because it indicates how bad the model is at predicting the target.

01:11:44.700 --> 01:11:49.700
Remember the difference between the two things, which is targets and predictions will be higher.

01:11:49.700 --> 01:11:53.700
And then the squares will be even higher and the average will be higher.

01:11:53.700 --> 01:11:57.700
And so the square root will be higher if the targets are very far away from the predictions.

01:11:57.700 --> 01:12:01.700
That means if your model is really bad, then the root mean squared error is going to be very high.

01:12:01.700 --> 01:12:05.700
That's why it's called a loss because it represents the information loss in the model.

01:12:05.700 --> 01:12:09.700
Remember, we are not capturing the actual relationship.

01:12:09.700 --> 01:12:12.700
We are simply modeling the relationship and all models are wrong.

