Now we say that, Hey, for calculating the medical charges, we give some weight to the age and some weight to the BMI.

01:37:00.700 --> 01:37:06.700
And then we have this other intercept term, which is simply to just move the line up or down.

01:37:06.700 --> 01:37:11.700
Of course, now this is no longer a line. It's linear in the sense that there is still a linear relationship.

01:37:11.700 --> 01:37:16.700
We're not doing squares or cubes or anything, but this becomes now a plane in three dimensions.

01:37:16.700 --> 01:37:22.700
Essentially, if you see the, if you put age BMI and charges on each dimension, this becomes a plane in three dimensions.

01:37:22.700 --> 01:37:31.700
So now we are working with the plane, but still called a linear regression, simply a linear combination or a weighted average of the agent BMI, the charges.

