So the inputs are from non-smoker DF.

01:37:43.700 --> 01:37:49.700
We take age and we take the body mass index and then the targets are simply the charges.

01:37:49.700 --> 01:37:56.700
The only change we made here is this, the way to train the model and create the model is the same.

01:37:56.700 --> 01:38:06.700
So you create linear regression, you call dot fit, and then you put in the inputs and the targets, no change here.

01:38:06.700 --> 01:38:09.700
It's automatically going to detect that now you have two columns of data.

01:38:09.700 --> 01:38:17.700
Then you generate predictions, generate predictions by passing the inputs into model dot predict.

01:38:17.700 --> 01:38:19.700
And then finally you compute the loss.

01:38:19.700 --> 01:38:22.700
So this is not something that you have to do strictly speaking.

01:38:22.700 --> 01:38:28.700
You just, once the model is trained at fit, you can make predictions on any new input data, right?

