02:35:30.700 --> 02:35:34.700
So we have the actual yes, no, yes, no answers of whether it will rain tomorrow.

02:35:34.700 --> 02:35:40.700
And we take the predictions, which are probabilities and we put them into this loss function called cross entropy.

02:35:40.700 --> 02:35:47.700
We run that through the optimization algorithm. Once again, the optimization algorithms like gradient descent least squares.

02:35:47.700 --> 02:35:57.700
There are many optimization algorithms, and that is able to then change the parameters or change the weights and biases of the model, the W1 W2, et cetera.

02:35:57.700 --> 02:36:01.700
So that the model now makes better predictions and gets a lower loss, right?

