So it's not a perfect 60, 20, 20 split, but we have still ensured that the test validation, that the validation and test set.

03:15:50.700 --> 03:15:59.700
Both contains both contain data for at least 12 months or entire calendar year, which means they see all the seasonality and they occur in the future after the training data.

03:15:59.700 --> 03:16:04.700
So which will more accurately reflect our models performance in the real world.

03:16:04.700 --> 03:16:09.700
So the whole purpose of test training, validation, et cetera, is to create a model.

03:16:09.700 --> 03:16:14.700
Whose performance can be reliably measured on how it will perform in the real world, right?

03:16:14.700 --> 03:16:18.700
We don't just want to get a higher accuracy just for the sake of reporting it.

03:16:18.700 --> 03:16:21.700
We want to create models that work well in the real world.

