03:28:46.700 --> 03:28:49.700
Now, machine learning models cannot work with missing data.

03:28:49.700 --> 03:28:53.700
Whenever you have a nan and you try to train a machine learning model, it's probably going to crash.

03:28:54.700 --> 03:28:58.700
So you need to fill these missing values with some valid values.

03:28:58.700 --> 03:29:01.700
And the process of filling missing values is called imputation.

03:29:02.700 --> 03:29:07.700
Now there are several techniques for imputation, but we will use the most basic technique here.

03:29:07.700 --> 03:29:11.700
And I'll let you check out some of the other techniques and we will try out some other techniques over time.

03:29:12.700 --> 03:29:17.700
But the most basic technique is to replace missing values with the average value in the column.

03:29:18.700 --> 03:29:22.700
And you can do this using the simple imputed class from SK learn dot impute.

03:29:22.700 --> 03:29:27.700
So what we want to do is we want to replace this nan with the average value in this column.

03:29:27.700 --> 03:29:31.700
And I think the average in this column, if we have just three rows is 17 plus five, 22 by two 11.

03:29:31.700 --> 03:29:34.700
So we have 11 here and the average in this column is six.

03:29:34.700 --> 03:29:35.700
So we have six here.

03:29:35.700 --> 03:29:37.700
The average in this column is just seven.

03:29:37.700 --> 03:29:38.700
So we'll just put seven here.

03:29:39.700 --> 03:29:40.700
So this is just a guess.

03:29:40.700 --> 03:29:44.700
It's obviously may not be correct, but you have a choice here.

03:29:44.700 --> 03:29:51.700
You can either throw away those rows, but if you have a lot of nan values in a certain column and you throw away those rows, you may lose a lot of data.

03:29:51.700 --> 03:29:56.700
So you just take a guess there and you think that, okay, maybe I replace it with the average.

03:29:56.700 --> 03:30:02.700
Sometimes you may choose to replace it with not, not the average, but maybe a fixed value and it can do that as well.

03:30:02.700 --> 03:30:05.700
Simple imputer has several strategies.

03:30:05.700 --> 03:30:07.700
Sometimes you may replace it by the mean.

03:30:07.700 --> 03:30:11.700
If you are by the median, if you think that there are outliers that may affect the average.

03:30:11.700 --> 03:30:22.700
For example, if you have an income column, it's always a good idea to replace it with a, with the median rather than the mean, because there will be outliers that may affect the average.

03:30:24.700 --> 03:30:25.700
Okay.

03:30:25.700 --> 03:30:32.700
So many different strategies we are going to use a simple strategy of filling in nan values with the average value in that column.

