04:32:08.200 --> 04:32:09.440
And that is what machine learning is.

04:32:09.440 --> 04:32:15.000
It is about taking data and using data to make predictions, but how do you make predictions

04:32:15.000 --> 04:32:16.000
from data?

04:32:16.000 --> 04:32:22.360
You assume a certain relationship between the inputs, which is the weather information

04:32:22.360 --> 04:32:26.040
for today and the output, which is whether it will rain tomorrow.

04:32:26.040 --> 04:32:28.560
And that relationship is called the model.

04:32:28.560 --> 04:32:32.920
And that model has some inherent parameters called weights of the model, which are initially

04:32:32.920 --> 04:32:34.600
randomly initialized.

04:32:34.600 --> 04:32:38.160
And then you train the model, which means that you make predictions, compare them with

04:32:38.160 --> 04:32:39.160
the actual data.

04:32:39.160 --> 04:32:43.600
And that's where you need labeled historical data or labeled data for whether it rained

04:32:43.600 --> 04:32:46.080
the next day for the last 10 years.

04:32:46.080 --> 04:32:51.200
And using that comparison, computer loss, reduce the loss using an optimization technique,

04:32:51.200 --> 04:32:53.160
make the models parameters better.

04:32:53.160 --> 04:32:57.080
And as the model gets better, then you evaluate the model, you interpret the model, and then

04:32:57.080 --> 04:32:59.560
you use the model in the real world.

04:32:59.560 --> 04:33:01.060
This is used for weather prediction.

